Topic: Lecturette (Speaking Test) 🎤🔥

👉 This is where your confidence + clarity + thinking is tested
👉 You speak alone in front of group & GTO

1️⃣ What is Lecturette?

👉 You will get:

4 topics
Choose 1 topic

⏱️ Time:

3 min → Prepare
3 min → Speak
🎤 Lecturette Environment
2️⃣ Types of Topics

👉 Usually from:

Current affairs
Social issues
Personal topics
Abstract topics

📌 Examples:

Social media impact
Women empowerment
My role model
Leadership
3️⃣ How to Structure Speech (VERY IMPORTANT)

👉 Follow this simple structure:

🔹 1. Introduction (20–30 sec)

👉 Define topic

Example:
“Good morning, today I will speak on leadership…”

🔹 2. Body (Main Content)

👉 Include:

2–3 points
Examples
🔹 3. Conclusion

👉 End strongly:
“Thus, leadership is essential for success…”

🧠 GOLDEN RULE

👉 Simple + clear + confident

4️⃣ How to Choose Topic

✅ Choose topic:

You know something about
Easy to speak

❌ Don’t choose:

Very difficult topic
Completely unknown topic
5️⃣ Delivery Tips (VERY IMPORTANT)

✅ Maintain eye contact
✅ Speak clearly
✅ Use hand gestures
✅ Stay confident

❌ Avoid:
Looking down
Saying “umm… ahh…”
Standing stiff
6️⃣ Common Mistakes

❌ Memorized speech
❌ No structure
❌ Speaking too fast
❌ Losing confidence mid-way

7️⃣ PRO STRATEGY (SELECTION SECRET)

👉 Even if content is average:

💥 Confidence + clarity = selection

8️⃣ Practice Task (DO NOW)

Speak for 2–3 minutes on:

👉 “Role of youth in nation building”

Follow:

Intro
2 points
Conclusion
🧠 SECRET TIP

👉 GTO checks:

How you think
How you express
How confident you are

👉 Not your English level ❌
👉 Your confidence level ✅

